    <catchword>Quæ</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">æqualium alterum tertio fuerit inæqua-</l>
    <l n="2">le, &amp; reliquum eidem erit inæquale. Si</l>
    <l n="3">inæqualibus æqualia addātur,tota erūt</l>
    <l n="4">inæqualia. Si inæqualibus æqualia sub-</l>
    <l n="5">ducantur, reliqua erunt inæqualia. Im-</l>
    <l n="6">par, est majus aut minus. Majus est,cu-</l>
    <l n="7">jus quantitas excedit.Proprię notę sunt-</l>
    <l n="8">hujus rationis,non solúm,sed etiā,cú-</l>
    <l n="9">mtúm,malo hoc quám illud, plus, quám.</l>
    <l n="10">Cicero pro Muræna:</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Tollitur é medio</i>—</l>
    <l n="12">nō solúm ista verbosa simulatio prudē-</l>
    <l n="13">tiæ,sed etiam illa domina rerum—</l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Sapientia vi geritur res:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Spernitur orator</i>—</l>
    <l n="16">non solúm odiosus in dicendo,aut lo-</l>
    <l n="17">quax, verumetiam—</l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>bonus:horridu' miles amatur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Hinc sumitur interdum Logica quæ-</l>
    <l n="20">dam gradatio climaci Rhetorico con-</l>
    <l n="21">juncta.Pro Mil. Neqj vero se populo so-</l>
    <l n="22">lúm,sed etiam senatui tradidit: neqj se-</l>
    <l n="23">natui modó, sed etiā publicis præsidiis</l>
    <l n="24">&amp; armis : neqj his tantúm, verumetiam-</l>
    <l n="25">ejus potestati, cui Senatus totam Rem-</l>
    <l n="26">pub. omnem Italiæ pubem, cuncta po-</l>
    <l n="27">puli Romani arma commiserat. 2. Agra.</l>
  </main_text>
